body:
It seems to be another way to get a bound function, with a different style. The if isRefined will still need to be done at every render().

Compared to what it is right now:

``` js
function toggleRefinement(helper, facetName, isRefined) {
  var action = isRefined ? 'remove' : 'add';

  helper[action + 'FacetRefinement'](facetName, true).search();
}
```

Is it worse or better I dunno the pros/cons, so cannot decide if there's a need to refactor using your method.

